F1.14 Review of A1.12 (874364a = B8: Fix findings N1, N2, and N3 in card store)

Review of commit 874364a (B8: "Fix findings N1, N2, and N3 in card store") which
modifies 4 files:

  - docs/logs/card-store-n1-n3-fixes.log     : 94 lines (audit of N1–N3 fixes)
  - docs/team.md                              : 30 lines (append/remove blocks)
  - mathd/src/card_store.rs                   : 19 lines added + 0 removed
  - mathd/tests/card_store.rs                 : 196 lines added + 1 removed

Verification:
  - All three fixes (N1, N2, N3) were proven with failing plants in scratch clone.
  - The fixes were committed on branch f1d4 and pushed to origin.

Findings:

F1 (N1: Explicit FailedDomain match arm in from_verdict without catch-all pattern).
  The B8 commit adds an explicit `Verdict::FailedDomain` match arm in
  `mathd/src/card_store.rs::from_verdict`, replacing the catch-all `_ =>` pattern.
  This ensures that `Verdict::FailedDomain` is explicitly handled with a descriptive
  error message (`VerdictNotVerified { reason: "Verdict is FailedDomain at {:?} (side
  {:?} undefined, defined value {}" ...}`), rather than being silently caught by a
  catch-all arm. A new test `test_all_verdict_variants_exhaustive_rejection` verifies
  that exactly one verdict variant (`Verified`) can produce a `VerifiedWitness`, and
  all others (`Failed`, `FailedDomain`, `Unverifiable`) are correctly rejected.
  The change is in `mathd/src/card_store.rs` lines 95-102 (replacing the catch-all
  with explicit FailedDomain handling).

F2 (N2: Add test asserting get(hash) returns the most recently inserted card in bucket).
  The B8 commit adds an exhaustive test `test_card_store_get_returns_most_recent_card_in_bucket`
  in `mathd/tests/card_store.rs`. This test verifies that when multiple cards share the
  same structural hash (canonically equivalent expressions like `x + 1` and `1 + x`),
  `store.get(hash)` returns the most recently inserted card (last-wins semantics), while
  `store.get_all(hash)` returns all cards in insertion order. The test inserts two
  canonically equivalent cards and asserts that `get` returns the second one with updated
  points_tested and max_relative_error values, and that `get_all` returns both in insertion
  order.

F3 (N3: Document and test with_promotion_threshold(0) clamping to 1).
  The B8 commit adds clamping logic in `mathd/src/card_store.rs::with_promotion_threshold`:
  `let threshold = if n == 0 { 1 } else { n };` ensuring that a promotion threshold of 0
  is clamped to 1. This prevents the card store from panicking or creating degenerate
  zero-exemplar candidates. A new test `test_card_store_promotion_threshold_zero_clamped_to_one`
  verifies: (1) threshold(0) is clamped to 1, and (2) the first insert with clamped threshold
  immediately emits a proposal with `MethodStatus::Proposed` and `card_count() == 1`. A
  separate assertion confirms that threshold(3) does NOT clamp (remains 3).

F4 (Plant verification). All three fixes were proven with failing plants in scratch clone.
The plant branches (plant/f1-*) have their built-in hostname plant disabled by
repro.yml's `contains(github.ref,'plant/')` → `if: false`, so the plants are only
detected by the explicit code changes, not by the workflow hostname check.

F5 (No workflow changes needed). The B8 commit only modifies mathd source and tests,
plus documentation/log files. No changes to .github/workflows/ were required.

